    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0321" n="315" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg315"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Stevens.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 19.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-03-06"><hi rendition="#italic">March 6,
                        1890</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>. I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 18 of the 10th ultimo, by which I learn that, contrary to the indications of
                    the first “returns” of the late elections in the Hawaiian Islands, the result
                    throughout the islands proves favorable to the “reform party” and the present
                    ministry.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
